.SH NAME
git-work-flow-log - Print the flows' history


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-work flow log [NAME] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the history of one flow, or of every flow: every operation, oldest
first and one JSON object per line, so it says who changed a flow, when, and
to what.

.PP
--format text prints one line per operation instead.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-f\fP, \fB--format\fP="json"
	Select the output formatting style. Valid values are [json,text]

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for log


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-work-flow(1)\fP
